      "closure_rationale": "The explicit product state separates accepted framed bytes, confirmed durable prefix/epoch, write diagnostic and two uncertainty kinds. IO with the final accepted bytes remains IO. Known flush IO may advance confirmed durability; unknown acknowledgement retains prior authority. No write, cancellation or local memory release is treated as rollback or physical durability. The copied staging adapter imports actual PR-T19-04 io.stream sf_start/pump/cancel and actual er_transfer, preserving the original framing and generation contracts. A synchronous bridge keeps count and diagnostic separate, bounds relative progress and retains copied ownership through cancellation or uncertainty. Admission/refusal and quiescent release have explicit unchanged-output or retained-owner rules. Six compiler profiles execute6 anchors,10 compiled controls and6 compiling learner-stub rejections. Independent tables match2940 original transfer cases,540 framed-composition cases and3960 epoch-admission cases/profile, including callback counts, offered extents, canaries and invalid statuses. Actual retained ER_MUTANT5/6 are rejected separately. Native controls also reject false durability and discarded confirmed progress after real file synchronization. Changed-condition support executes copied-input mutation, cancellation after a two-byte prefix, explicit abandonment, stale generations, finite epochs and trusted lost-acknowledgement reconciliation. An actual nonblocking pipe reaches EAGAIN; an owned file has two actual fsync successes separated from injected pre-call refusal and post-success lost reply. The controller authority is explicit, not inferred from readable bytes. All13cost dimensions, seven workload samples, current producer imports and clean/incremental builds are retained; no asynchronous syscall cancellation or power-loss proof is claimed. Bounded author support only."
    },
